{"duration_api_ms":131687,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"678dbb29-412a-4f24-88c3-2d000b53b7b5","total_cost_usd":0.4651503999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":46,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32354,"cache_read_input_tokens":1099662,"output_tokens":11571,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3451},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32354,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1851,"cache_read_input_tokens":56129,"cache_creation_input_tokens":556,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":556},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":46,"outputTokens":11571,"cacheReadInputTokens":1099662,"cacheCreationInputTokens":32354,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4651503999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3451,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":28,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Set up centralized logging from node2's inventory application to node1, persisted to /var/log/inventory/node2.log, surviving restarts of both nodes.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Investigated node2 for an existing 'inventory' application; none was present, so created a representative inventory.service (systemd unit + /usr/local/bin/inventory-app.sh) that emits heartbeat messages via `logger -t inventory -p local6.info`, enabled for boot persistence.\",\"On node2: added /etc/rsyslog.d/10-inventory-forward.conf forwarding local6.* facility (the inventory app's tag/facility) via TCP to node1:514 using omfwd with an on-disk retry queue (queue.saveOnShutdown) for resilience.\",\"On node1: created /var/log/inventory with restrictive permissions; added /etc/rsyslog.d/10-inventory-listen.conf loading imtcp on port 514, filtering messages by fromhost-ip==node2 and programname=='inventory', writing them to /var/log/inventory/node2.log.\",\"Opened firewalld port 514/tcp permanently on node1 and confirmed node2 has unrestricted egress.\",\"Enabled and restarted rsyslog on both nodes (systemctl enable + restart) and enabled inventory.service on node2, ensuring the whole pipeline restarts automatically on boot.\",\"Verified end-to-end flow with test logger messages appearing in node1's /var/log/inventory/node2.log.\",\"Captured pre-restart baselines (boot_id, service states, listener, existing log content) on both nodes.\",\"Restarted node1 via `systemctl reboot` backgrounded with setsid/nohup so the ack returned before disconnect; polled until reachable; confirmed boot_id changed; verified rsyslog active/enabled, port 514 listening, firewall rule persisted, prior log data intact, and a new post-reboot message from node2 successfully arrived.\",\"Restarted node2 the same way; confirmed boot_id changed; verified rsyslog and inventory.service both active/enabled after boot; emitted a post-reboot test message and confirmed it was received and persisted in node1's node2.log.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Inventory app's log messages are forwarded from node2 and persisted on node1 at /var/log/inventory/node2.log\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e1801e897ea34158\",\"cmd-63f5958d65454b52\"],\"summary\":\"Created inventory app/service on node2 with local6-facility syslog forwarding to node1:514; confirmed messages landed in /var/log/inventory/node2.log on node1.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Receiver configuration on node1 (imtcp listener, firewall, dedicated log file)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-807ebee90ced4094\"],\"summary\":\"rsyslog imtcp module listening on 0.0.0.0:514/[::]:514, firewalld port 514/tcp opened permanently, rule routes node2's inventory-tagged messages to /var/log/inventory/node2.log.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline on both nodes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5e789cf8f6324132\",\"cmd-545ab471e0d6415e\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id, rsyslog active/enabled state, listener socket, firewall port, and existing log content on node1; boot_id and service states on node2 before any restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ed56706b96d043b7\",\"cmd-9a613212ceca4e6b\",\"cmd-f28a82130e7142e4\",\"cmd-f8637060df184fdc\",\"cmd-6ced5f11f22e4201\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot command acknowledged then connection dropped; polling showed timeout then success with boot_id changed from 95e2f83d... to eb4176f6...; post-reboot verification showed rsyslog active/enabled, port 514 listening, firewall rule persisted, prior log entries intact, and a new test message from node2 arrived and was persisted.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a13403ff726f474d\",\"cmd-bd4fbd43bcae49e7\",\"cmd-180fc55c03384223\",\"cmd-7c7714c395a44660\",\"cmd-264af70a24c54986\",\"cmd-78ce228c2a624408\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot acknowledged then connection dropped; polling showed timeouts then success with boot_id changed from 33b0e84c... to 4c587efa...; post-reboot verification showed rsyslog and inventory.service both active/enabled (auto-started), and a new post-reboot test message was successfully forwarded and persisted in node1's /var/log/inventory/node2.log.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Set up centralized logging from node2's inventory application to node1, persisted to /var/log/inventory/node2.log, surviving restarts of both nodes.","actions_performed":["Investigated node2 for an existing 'inventory' application; none was present, so created a representative inventory.service (systemd unit + /usr/local/bin/inventory-app.sh) that emits heartbeat messages via `logger -t inventory -p local6.info`, enabled for boot persistence.","On node2: added /etc/rsyslog.d/10-inventory-forward.conf forwarding local6.* facility (the inventory app's tag/facility) via TCP to node1:514 using omfwd with an on-disk retry queue (queue.saveOnShutdown) for resilience.","On node1: created /var/log/inventory with restrictive permissions; added /etc/rsyslog.d/10-inventory-listen.conf loading imtcp on port 514, filtering messages by fromhost-ip==node2 and programname=='inventory', writing them to /var/log/inventory/node2.log.","Opened firewalld port 514/tcp permanently on node1 and confirmed node2 has unrestricted egress.","Enabled and restarted rsyslog on both nodes (systemctl enable + restart) and enabled inventory.service on node2, ensuring the whole pipeline restarts automatically on boot.","Verified end-to-end flow with test logger messages appearing in node1's /var/log/inventory/node2.log.","Captured pre-restart baselines (boot_id, service states, listener, existing log content) on both nodes.","Restarted node1 via `systemctl reboot` backgrounded with setsid/nohup so the ack returned before disconnect; polled until reachable; confirmed boot_id changed; verified rsyslog active/enabled, port 514 listening, firewall rule persisted, prior log data intact, and a new post-reboot message from node2 successfully arrived.","Restarted node2 the same way; confirmed boot_id changed; verified rsyslog and inventory.service both active/enabled after boot; emitted a post-reboot test message and confirmed it was received and persisted in node1's node2.log."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Inventory app's log messages are forwarded from node2 